From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:07:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [DS4.1] Expert scale codes: a narrow expert's 2-bit codes
 replace its 4-bit codes in one buffer

The 2-bit codes had their own buffer, half the 4-bit codes' size, for every
expert, beside 4-bit codes that were also kept for every expert: about
1 GiB more weights a rank at TP4 than candidate 10. A narrow expert's rows
of the 4-bit buffer now hold its 2-bit bytes (the first block_N bytes of
each row, zeros after), and the GEMM reads them through a uint8 view of
the same storage, [rows, 2 * block_N]. A wide expert keeps its 4-bit rows.
Each narrow load is still one contiguous block_N-byte row, so the bytes
read and the expanded scale words, and so every output bit, are unchanged.
